        <mda:meta type="pos_id">31</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="reviewed">
        <source>::You start to pulverize the rocks but - they don't go down without a fight. The blockade shatters piece by piece, leaving nothing behind. As the cloud of dust settles, you see that there is still more in your way: a huge wall of junk. You take one deep breath before continuing to dig through. In doing so, an overwhelming thick gas, for a brief moment, clogs the air channels in your neck, causing you to pause for a moment. With every gasp thereafter, you can feel the flow of air as it sands your throat, causing aggravating sensation all the way through in both directions. This pain motivates you to sweep away the remaining trash ahead with ease.:: &lt;end&gt;</source>
